can: af_can: export can_sock_destruct()

jira KERNEL-1078
cve CVE-2026-31532
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.126.1.el8_10
commit-author Oleksij Rempel <o.rempel@pengutronix.de>
commit 975987e7015bb12a482df7f14fd524417d2c8e8f
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.126.1.el8_10/975987e7.failed

In j1939 we need our own struct sock::sk_destruct callback. Export the
generic af_can can_sock_destruct() that allows us to chain-call it.

Fixes: 9d71dd0c7009 ("can: add support of SAE J1939 protocol")
	Signed-off-by: Oleksij Rempel <o.rempel@pengutronix.de>
(cherry picked from commit 975987e7015bb12a482df7f14fd524417d2c8e8f)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	include/linux/can/core.h
